course: dictionary
lesson: 906
title: Black in many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word black can mean different things, so read the words around it to find the right one. «It was black outside» means there was no light, so it was dark. The clue is that it was outside, and nobody could see.
explain: Black is also a colour: the darkest one, like coal or the night sky. «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears» tells you the ears are the colour black, not dark.
explain: Sometimes black is part of a phrase. «Black box» is a set of words that means one thing together, so it is not just black plus box. A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Black is the darkest colour, the colour of coal and the night sky.
fact: «Black» can also mean with no light, as in «It was black outside».
fact: Mixing black into a colour makes a shade, which is a darker version of that colour.
fact: «Black coffee» means coffee with no milk.
fact: Black can describe people whose families came from Africa, so use the word with care and respect.
exercise: «It was black outside when we walked home.» What does black mean here? | Covered in paint | Full of milk | *With no light | Very cold
exercise: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears.» What colour are the backs of the tiger's ears? | *Black | Pink | Green | Brown
exercise: What does «black coffee» mean? | Coffee that has been burnt black | Coffee drunk only at night | Coffee served in a black cup | *Coffee with no milk
test: In Chinese, «hēi» also means dark, as in «tiān hēi le» (it's got dark). Which word means dark? | loud | early | *dark | hot
test: Which phrase means something written down? | black eye | blackout | *in black and white | blackboard
exam: «Ukraine's black earth, chornozem, was built over thousands of years.» What helped build it? | *Steppe grass roots dying and rotting into the ground | Snow melting in spring | Volcanoes erupting | Rain falling for one year
